# oracle: compute pe/atom and stress/atom (pair terms) with pair hybrid/overlay lj/cut + hbond/dreiding/lj (the w14hbond_lj system, 5 hydrogen bonds): each donor-hydrogen-acceptor term gives a third of its energy and of its virial to each of the three atoms (native ev_tally3), dumps at the start and the end
# Measured max relative error, engine vs native (thermo rows, final atoms): thermo 2.3e-13, atoms 9.3e-13 (the dumped per-atom values included; the 100-step trajectory of w14hbond_lj).
# oracle-inputs: w14hbond_system.data
# oracle-files: w274hb_lj_peratom.dump
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-10 abs=1e-10 filerel=1e-9
units           real
atom_style      full
boundary        p p p
read_data       w14hbond_system.data
special_bonds   lj/coul 0.0 0.0 1.0
pair_style      hybrid/overlay lj/cut 8.0 hbond/dreiding/lj 4 3.0 4.5 90.0
pair_coeff      * * lj/cut 0.1 2.8
pair_coeff      1 3 hbond/dreiding/lj 2 i 2.0 2.2
pair_coeff      1 5 hbond/dreiding/lj 2 i 1.5 2.4 2 3.0 4.5 90.0
bond_style      harmonic
bond_coeff      1 450.0 0.9572
bond_coeff      2 300.0 1.2
neighbor        2.0 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
timestep        1.0
fix             1 all nve
thermo_style    custom step pe evdwl ebond press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          20
compute         pa all pe/atom pair
compute         sa all stress/atom NULL pair
dump            d all custom 100 w274hb_lj_peratom.dump id c_pa c_sa[1] c_sa[2] c_sa[3] c_sa[4] c_sa[5] c_sa[6]
dump_modify     d sort id format float %.15g
run             100
